Notebook[{
Cell["Unit 4 \[CenterDot] Building Our Own Net", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b3517a66-cb51-41bb-9b6f-919428b971cb"],

Cell["\<\
A transformer that expands \:2a02/\:2a01 expressions, assembled from Units 1\
\[Dash]3 \[LongDash] TensorNets units of learning, 4 of 4\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"45318a38-328d-4624-87e0-4abdc16aa9bf"],

Cell["\[Copyright] 2026 Computational Classnotes \[CenterDot] CC BY-NC-SA \
4.0", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5020c19-a4b1-472a-92f4-04c3af889028"],

Cell["\<\
This unit puts Units 1\[Dash]3 to work on our own problem. Given an \
expression such as (a\:2a01b)\:2a02c, the net must write its expansion \
a\:2a02c \:2a01 b\:2a02c. The data come from Unit 2 (uniform trees, prefix \
notation, an exact checker), the net from Unit 3 (attention, feed-forward, \
LayerNorm, positions, shared embeddings, label smoothing, warm-up), and the \
decoding from Units 1 and 3 (beam search with a length penalty). Evaluate \
from top to bottom; training (\[Section]6) takes about five minutes on a \
laptop CPU. The write-up \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Unit 4 \[CenterDot] Building \
Our Own Net\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] has the same section numbers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58ccf077-490c-479b-bb58-7524986cfbc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before you start: choose Evaluation \[RightPointer] Quit Kernel \
\[RightPointer] Local. To skip training, evaluate \[Section]1, then the \
notebook unit4_",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["build", "your"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a228253f-4a40-42f3-a184-67c4e30b6e14"],
 "_",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["own", "nets"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "46f9cb71-81ff-4e0d-a7f2-a33c614c0b85"],
 ".nb (it defines ownNet), and continue from \[Section]7."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2aa7772-495a-49fc-b785-3ed222c039d5"],

Cell["1. Toolkit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b0362d64-e56a-4acb-a6fb-ed2fcdc3a978"],

Cell["\<\
Data and oracle (\[Section]3, \[Section]4): binaryTree samples uniform binary \
trees, parseT reads prefix tokens into a tree, infix writes a tree with the \
fewest parentheses, words and expand compute the exact expansion, equivalentQ \
checks an answer. The net (\[Section]5): the parts of Unit 3, and model, \
which assembles them. Training (\[Section]6): train, with label smoothing and \
the warm-up schedule. Decoding (\[Section]7): beamSearch, with or without the \
prefix grammar.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9619c25a-f495-4bd6-98e2-a0841f56276b"],

