Cell["2. The task: expand", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"583d2b7c-430f-4f78-acbd-a8dbfb7bf4be"],

Cell["\<\
\:2a02 distributes over \:2a01 on both sides: (A\:2a01B)\:2a02C = A\:2a02C \
\:2a01 B\:2a02C and A\:2a02(B\:2a01C) = A\:2a02B \:2a01 A\:2a02C. Expanding \
writes an expression as a \:2a01 of words, each word a \:2a02-product of \
atoms. The source is the expression as one would type it; the target is the \
expansion in prefix notation (Unit 2). The target can be much longer than the \
source: each \:2a02 of two sums multiplies the number of words.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b38f989d-d241-4e89-9c60-10c09c5fcdc6"],

