Cell["\<\
Check: {14, True, min, max}: the sampler reaches all 14 binary trees with \
four operators, each close to 1000 times in 14 000 samples.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"663dcc60-65bc-4d51-902d-8f3135e4d084"],

Cell["4. The oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"25b17387-f29c-431e-ad65-5e4e1987db38"],

Cell["\<\
An expression is a list of words. \:2a01 joins two lists. \:2a02 multiplies \
every word on the left by every word on the right, keeping their order, \
because \:2a02 is not commutative. Two expressions are equal when their lists \
of words agree up to order (\:2a01 is commutative up to isomorphism). This is \
the check tnEquivalentQ makes in TensorNets.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b03c7aac-e43c-4b20-b784-aa220e7c2a68"],

Cell["\<\
words(x) = {x}      words(A \:2a01 B) = words(A) \:222a words(B)      words(A \
\:2a02 B) = { u v : u \[Element] words(A), v \[Element] words(B) }\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"3a0d7301-6b97-4593-8487-be028fa6c637"],

Cell["\<\
(a\:2a01b)\:2a02(c\:2a01d): words(a\:2a01b) = {a, b} and words(c\:2a01d) = \
{c, d}, so the product gives {ac, ad, bc, bd}: four words of two atoms. In \
prefix, as a right-nested sum of right-nested products: \:2a01 \:2a02 a c \
\:2a01 \:2a02 a d \:2a01 \:2a02 b c \:2a02 b d, 15 tokens from a source of 11.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"c18323c7-b2d2-47e7-9d47-7a42ab4ff533"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"id", ":", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"9106", "b79c"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"33", "c4"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"42", "ed"}], "-", "a256", "-", 
     RowBox[{"6", 
