Cell["\<\
Check: {True, False, True}: a\:2a02c \:2a01 b\:2a02c is accepted in either \
order; c\:2a02a \:2a01 c\:2a02b is rejected, since the order of factors \
matters; and for 500 random pairs the target is equivalent to the source.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5be4cc9f-ac51-4161-a003-7305a2ed2f5b"],

Cell["5. The net, assembled from Unit 3", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5d81509b-6420-442b-834a-27032daaf6c8"],

Cell["\<\
The encoder\[Dash]decoder of Unit 3, small: d = 32, 4 heads, dff = 128, 2 \
encoder and 2 decoder layers. Source and target share one vocabulary of 10 \
tokens, so one array serves the encoder embedding, the decoder embedding and \
the output projection. The decoder reads the target without its last token \
and predicts it without its first (teacher forcing). A frozen EmbeddingLayer \
whose rows are the smoothed targets turns each target index into the \
label-smoothed distribution (\[CurlyEpsilon] = 0.1), and the loss is the \
cross-entropy against it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc3a0964-eaa2-4205-804c-0857bc77983c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"id", ":", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"5", "aae147d"}], "-", 
