Cell["\<\
Check: {0.500, first loss, last loss, True, True}: the loss fell by more than \
half and stays above the floor.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dfa7a242-b31f-4f1f-9064-84cdb08d5288"],

Cell["7. Decoding and checking", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"51ebe5d2-0064-4fc2-b01c-65b0e675e3c5"],

Cell["\<\
Each test source is decoded three ways: greedy (a beam of width 1); a beam of \
width 4 with the length penalty \[Alpha] = 0.6; and the same beam constrained \
by the prefix grammar. The grammar uses Unit 2\[CloseCurlyQuote]s counter: \
</s> is allowed only when the tree is complete, and nothing else is allowed \
then. Every answer is checked by the oracle. As in Lample and Charton, \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]any in beam\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] counts a source as \
solved if any hypothesis in the beam passes the check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f906c70-2217-45c7-b496-aa3fc3f8ad75"],

Cell["\<\
After \:2a01 a the counter is 1 + (2 \[Minus] 1) + (0 \[Minus] 1) = 1: one \
subtree is still owed, so </s> is forbidden and an atom or an operator must \
follow. After \:2a01 a b it is 0: the tree is complete, and only </s> is \
allowed.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"f46e0142-ca2d-4b77-9db0-a795edb9d668"],

